Third-party material
================================================================================

obra/superpowers — https://github.com/obra/superpowers
Copyright (c) 2025 Jesse Vincent
MIT License — full text in vendor/superpowers/LICENSE

No superpowers file is redistributed verbatim. Two things here are adapted from it:

    payload/claude/workflow/testing.md
        Its principles — name the break a test catches, derive expectations by hand,
        exercise the real thing, the mutation check — are adapted from superpowers'
        skills/test-driven-development/writing-good-tests.md (v6.3.0), rewritten for
        outcome tests.

    payload/claude/skills/batch-implement/SKILL.md, payload/claude/agents/*.md
        The process ideas — task briefs instead of pasted history, a run log that survives
        compaction, rulings recorded instead of stalls, a short fixed report contract — are
        adapted from superpowers' subagent-driven-development skill (v6.3.0). The execution
        model differs: tasks run in parallel, tests and code are written by separate agents,
        and a task is gated by tests rather than by per-task review.

mattpocock/skills — https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
Copyright (c) 2026 Matt Pocock
MIT License

No file is redistributed verbatim. One thing here is adapted from it:

    payload/claude/skills/knowledge-layer/CONTEXT-FORMAT.md
        The CONTEXT.md glossary format — a term, a one or two sentence definition of what it
        is, and an opinionated `_Avoid_` list naming the synonyms it beats — is adapted from
        skills/engineering/domain-modeling/CONTEXT-FORMAT.md. The decision half of that skill
        is deliberately not carried over: decisions here live in docs/decisions/, written by
        /spec and /batch-implement, and /knowledge-layer only links into them.

